------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository depends on, but does not include, the following external
projects. Their own licenses apply.

pipecat (git submodule, https://github.com/dograh-hq/pipecat.git)
    BSD 2-Clause. The upstream Dograh fork of pipecat publishes the
    `pipecat.services.dograh.*` service classes. Bolo imports these symbols
    under their upstream names, because the module lives in a separate
    repository that Bolo does not own. Renaming them requires forking pipecat
    as well.

Dograh Managed Platform Services (MPS)
    The default value of `MPS_API_URL` points at the upstream managed service
    host (`https://services.dograh.com`), which is an external SaaS endpoint
    operated by Zansat Technologies Private Limited. It is not part of this
    source tree. Point `MPS_API_URL` at your own deployment to use a
    self-hosted equivalent.

Community MinIO build
    The bundled MinIO image (`dograhai/minio`) is a community build published
    by github.com/dograh-hq/minio, used because upstream MinIO no longer
    publishes images. Its own license applies.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Brand assets
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Bolo logo, mark, inverse lockup, watermark imprint and favicon are original
artwork created for this fork and are generated by
scripts/brand/generate_brand_assets.py. They are not derived from the upstream
Dograh brand assets.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modifications made in this fork
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

* Renamed the product, packages, environment variables, container images,
  Helm chart, SDK package names, routes and URLs from "Dograh" to "Bolo".
* Replaced the upstream brand artwork with original Bolo artwork.
* Re-based the UI design system on a teal-green palette (light and dark).
* Renamed the documentation set and refreshed the README.
